## Failed alternatives the audience has tried (DRAFT, validate with real installers)
Contact forms that return "call me" leads; WhatsApp back and forth for a price; PDF/Excel price lists emailed by hand; generic quote
software that does not know windows (profiles, glass, openings); a configurator from the manufacturer that sends the lead to the
manufacturer; paying for ads that bring price shoppers.

## Avatars (DRAFT)
1. Owner of a small installer firm, 40-55, does quotes at night. 2. Showroom salesperson 28-38. 3. Back-office coordinator 30-45.
4. Second-generation owner 24-32, digital-friendly. 5. Dealer network manager 35-50 (Agency/Enterprise angle).

## Pain points
- Surface: "clienti che chiedono solo il prezzo e spariscono"; "preventivi che fanno perdere ore".
- Deep (mass-desire in the trade): the mental tax of rebuilding the same quote at 10 pm; the time pain of chasing a customer who never
  signs; the "I have optimised everything else" pain of an owner whose site still brings only calls; the recognition pain of a
  professional shop whose website looks like a brochure from 2012; public-visibility pain of a slow or messy quote in front of a client
  at the showroom counter.

## Funnel stage mapping
Cold (installers who do not know the tool) → **Full Stack**. Warm (visited the site, tried the demo, abandoned the sign-up) →
**Mid-Funnel Punchy**. Product-hero scale tests without talent → **Animated Infomercial** built from real screen captures.

## Plans (for CTA context only; confirm before quoting any price)
Widget family: Level 1 (49.95 €/month), Level 2 (62.44), Level 3 (79.90). Platform family: Base 97, Pro 197 (trial), Agency 397,
Enterprise 690 (per month, VAT excluded). Source of truth: onespec.eu/prezzi and `convex/lib/billingPlans.ts`.

## Asset checklist (ASK Stefan / capture)
- Logo (SVG/PNG, dark and light), brand colours (mint `#16d19d` family), fonts used on the site.
- Real captures: dashboard, configurator with a priced window, quote PDF with signature, widget inside a dealer-style site, leads import.
- Voice: preferred AI voice (Higgsfield voices or other) and locale per market.
- Whether any real customer is willing to appear or be quoted (needed for any true testimonial).
- Platform accounts for posting (TikTok, Instagram, YouTube) and the AI-content labelling choice.
